request.description:
When any request answers **401 `token_expired`**: renew, then send that request again, once. No `Authorization` header is needed.

**200**: a new access pass **and a new refresh pass** (both saved for you). In the app, store both before anything else.

**Renew once at a time.** A refresh pass works exactly once: sending one again ends the login (we must assume it was copied). When several requests fail together, they all wait for the same single renewal:

```ts
let renewing: Promise<boolean> | null = null;
function renewOnce(): Promise<boolean> {
  renewing ??= api('auth/refresh', { refresh_token: store.refreshToken })
    .then(async (r) => { if (!r.ok) return false; await store.save((await r.json()).data); return true; })
    .finally(() => { renewing = null; });
  return renewing;
}
```

| HTTP | `error.code` | When | In the app |
|---|---|---|---|
| 401 | `unauthenticated` | the login ended (30 days unused, logged out, blocked, password changed elsewhere, a pass used twice) | the login screen |

Guide §3.3, §3.4.

